From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <DCHEM88@hotmail.it>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 04:18:59 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] northbridge/intel/haswell: Retrain after the rank mapping fix

The rank mapping fix (CB:96694, the previous commit) changes the 1D
margin training of ranks 1-3, which ran with the register file of rank
0 before it. A training saved by the old code in RW_MRC_CACHE still
passes every fast boot check, which compare only the DIMMs and the CPU
(restore_non_training()), so the fixed code would boot on the old
margins without ever training them again.

Today the W541 empties RW_MRC_CACHE wherever it changes the code: a
capsule, update.py other-slot and the setup's "Go back to" (smmstore
keeps the cache only with SMMSTORE_VBOOT_SWITCH_KEEPS_MRC_CACHE, which
only the M920x selects). Not on a vboot fallback: when the slot on
trial runs out of tries, the other slot boots on the cache that the
first one saved, and with one slot before the fix and one after, each
would use the other's training. A slot written with flashrom alone, or
a later change that keeps the cache on the W541 as on the M920x, would
do the same.

Bump reg_frame_rev() to 3, as "Haswell NRI: Fix per-bit sense amp
offset packing" bumped it to 2: mrc_cache then sees another version and
the memory is trained once more, and each slot ignores the other's
data. It is kept out of the backport, which stays as upstream has it.
It costs one training on the first boot of a slot with this commit,
which the W541 does anyway after a capsule.

TEST=Host syntax check with -Werror and the ci-150 W541 nri config.
Still to test on the W541 (nri): with a training of an older nri build
left in RW_MRC_CACHE (only the RW slot written), the first boot logs
"MRC: version mismatch: 2 vs 3" and trains, the next one logs "Using
cached memory parameters"; after a vboot fallback to an older nri slot,
that slot also trains once ("version mismatch: 3 vs 2").

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../intel/haswell/native_raminit/save_restore.c            | 7 +++++--
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/native_raminit/save_restore.c b/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/native_raminit/save_restore.c
index 6e199d3441..da737d2927 100644
--- a/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/native_raminit/save_restore.c
+++ b/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/native_raminit/save_restore.c
@@ -16,9 +16,12 @@ uint32_t reg_frame_rev(void)
 	 * require invalidating the cache.
 	 *
 	 * Exception: revision 2 discards data saved with broken per-bit
-	 * sense amplifier offsets, so that they get trained again.
+	 * sense amplifier offsets, so that they get trained again. Revision
+	 * 3 does the same for data saved before the rank mapping fix
+	 * (CB:96694), whose 1D margins of ranks 1-3 were trained with the
+	 * register file of rank 0.
 	 */
-	return 2;
+	return 3;
 }
 
 struct register_save {
